    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187A(3C) Service providers must keep certain information and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that\nincludes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:\n\n(a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint\nCommittee on Intelligence and Security for review; and\n\n(b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which\nthe Committee is to report on its review, a period that will\nend earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament\nafter the introduction of the Bill.",
      "skos:definition": "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that\nincludes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:\n\n(a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint\nCommittee on Intelligence and Security for review; and\n\n(b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which\nthe Committee is to report on its review, a period that will\nend earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament\nafter the introduction of the Bill.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9061571d5e9f4bc7d80887a7e3bc13dad83b5699a4939e05081fe890d3c360a2",
      "skos:note": "Must refer amendment to Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security for review.",
      "dc:description": "Review report within 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187A(3C) Service providers must keep certain information and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that\nincludes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:\n\n(a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint\nCommittee on Intelligence and Security for review; and\n\n(b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which\nthe Committee is to report on its review, a period that will\nend earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament\nafter the introduction of the Bill."
    },
