    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187B Certain service providers not covered by this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subsection 187A(1) does not apply to a service provider (other\nthan a carrier that is not a carriage service provider) in relation to a\nrelevant service that it operates if:\n\n(a) the service:\n\n(i) is provided only to a person’s immediate circle (within\nthe meaning of section 23 of the Telecommunications\nAct 1997); or\n\n(ii) is provided only to places that, under section 36 of that\nAct, are all in the same area; and\n\n(b) the service is not subject to a declaration under subsection (2)\nof this section.\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator may declare that\nsubsection 187A(1) applies in relation to a relevant service that a\nservice provider operates.\n\n(2A) Before a declaration is made, a Communications Access\nCoordinator may consult the Privacy Commissioner.\n\n(3) In considering whether to make a declaration, a Communications\nAccess Coordinator must have regard to:\n\n(a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and\n\n(b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(ba) the objects of the Privacy Act 1988; and\n\n(bb) any submissions made by the Privacy Commissioner because\nof the consultation under subsection (2A); and\n\n(c) any other matter that the Coordinator considers relevant.\n\n(4) The declaration must be in writing.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nData retention  Part 5-1A\nObligation to keep information and documents  Division 1\n\nSection 187BA\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(5) A declaration made under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after a declaration is made under\nsubsection (2), a Communications Access Coordinator must give\nwritten notice of the declaration to the Minister.\n\n(7) As soon as practicable after receiving the notice under\nsubsection (6), the Minister must give written notice of the\ndeclaration to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence\nand Security.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subsection 187A(1) does not apply to a service provider (other\nthan a carrier that is not a carriage service provider) in relation to a\nrelevant service that it operates if:\n\n(a) the service:\n\n(i) is provided only to a person’s immediate circle (within\nthe meaning of section 23 of the Telecommunications\nAct 1997); or\n\n(ii) is provided only to places that, under section 36 of that\nAct, are all in the same area; and\n\n(b) the service is not subject to a declaration under subsection (2)\nof this section.\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator may declare that\nsubsection 187A(1) applies in relation to a relevant service that a\nservice provider operates.\n\n(2A) Before a declaration is made, a Communications Access\nCoordinator may consult the Privacy Commissioner.\n\n(3) In considering whether to make a declaration, a Communications\nAccess Coordinator must have regard to:\n\n(a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and\n\n(b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(ba) the objects of the Privacy Act 1988; and\n\n(bb) any submissions made by the Privacy Commissioner because\nof the consultation under subsection (2A); and\n\n(c) any other matter that the Coordinator considers relevant.\n\n(4) The declaration must be in writing.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nData retention  Part 5-1A\nObligation to keep information and documents  Division 1\n\nSection 187BA\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(5) A declaration made under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after a declaration is made under\nsubsection (2), a Communications Access Coordinator must give\nwritten notice of the declaration to the Minister.\n\n(7) As soon as practicable after receiving the notice under\nsubsection (6), the Minister must give written notice of the\ndeclaration to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence\nand Security.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187b-ss-1"
        },
