    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187L Confidentiality of applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a Communications Access Coordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Coordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than another Communications Access Coordinator, the\nACMA, an enforcement agency or a security authority)\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than a Communications Access Coordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a Communications Access Coordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Coordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than another Communications Access Coordinator, the\nACMA, an enforcement agency or a security authority)\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than a Communications Access Coordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "96a2623f16aa659ba1a72b2dddb603ece2538b204824a98db232341e71ad3b3f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187L Confidentiality of applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a Communications Access Coordinator receives a service\nprovider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data\nretention implementation plan, or application for a decision under\nsubsection 187K(1), the Coordinator must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than another Communications Access Coordinator, the\nACMA, an enforcement agency or a security authority)\nwithout the written permission of the service provider.\n\n(1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under\nsection 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1),\nthe ACMA must:\n\n(a) treat the application as confidential; and\n\n(b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body\n(other than a Communications Access Coordinator, an\nenforcement agency or a security authority) without the\nwritten permission of the service provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"
    },
