    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187M Pecuniary penalties and infringement notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "Subsection 187A(1) and paragraph 187D(a) are civil penalty\nprovisions for the purposes of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote:\nParts 31 and 31B of the Telecommunications Act 1997 provide for\npecuniary penalties and infringement notices for contraventions of\ncivil penalty provisions.",
      "skos:definition": "Subsection 187A(1) and paragraph 187D(a) are civil penalty\nprovisions for the purposes of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote:\nParts 31 and 31B of the Telecommunications Act 1997 provide for\npecuniary penalties and infringement notices for contraventions of\ncivil penalty provisions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51ebcb975cc272fa938244b05f56765b0874cdd3744d5e69f40200d74af646b6",
      "skos:note": "Pecuniary penalties and infringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187M Pecuniary penalties and infringement notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "Subsection 187A(1) and paragraph 187D(a) are civil penalty\nprovisions for the purposes of the Telecommunications Act 1997.\nNote:\nParts 31 and 31B of the Telecommunications Act 1997 provide for\npecuniary penalties and infringement notices for contraventions of\ncivil penalty provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187m-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits pecuniary penalties and infringement notices.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "187N Review of operation of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security\nmust review the operation of this Part.\n\n(1A) The review:\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nData retention  Part 5-1A\nMiscellaneous  Division 4\n\nSection 187P\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) must start on or before the second anniversary of the end of\nthe implementation phase; and\n\n(b) must be concluded on or before the third anniversary of the\nend of the implementation phase.\n\n(2) The Committee must give the Minister a written report of the\nreview.\n\n(3) Until the review is completed, the head (however described) of an\nenforcement agency must keep:\n\n(a) all of the documents that he or she is required to retain under\nsection 185; and\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 186(1)(e) to (k), to include in a report under\nsubsection 186(1);\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(4) Until the review is completed, the Director-General of Security\nmust keep:\n\n(a) all of the authorisations made under Division 3 of Part 4-1;\nand\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 94(2A)(c) to (j) of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979, to include in a report\nreferred to in subsection 94(1) of that Act;\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not limit any other obligation to keep\ninformation under this Act or another law.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security\nmust review the operation of this Part.\n\n(1A) The review:\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nData retention  Part 5-1A\nMiscellaneous  Division 4\n\nSection 187P\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) must start on or before the second anniversary of the end of\nthe implementation phase; and\n\n(b) must be concluded on or before the third anniversary of the\nend of the implementation phase.\n\n(2) The Committee must give the Minister a written report of the\nreview.\n\n(3) Until the review is completed, the head (however described) of an\nenforcement agency must keep:\n\n(a) all of the documents that he or she is required to retain under\nsection 185; and\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 186(1)(e) to (k), to include in a report under\nsubsection 186(1);\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(4) Until the review is completed, the Director-General of Security\nmust keep:\n\n(a) all of the authorisations made under Division 3 of Part 4-1;\nand\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 94(2A)(c) to (j) of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979, to include in a report\nreferred to in subsection 94(1) of that Act;\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not limit any other obligation to keep\ninformation under this Act or another law.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187n-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ea1cadc57bf8a7764a2660287ebca97e8497de147f3eefbde9a5579ca5ffd45c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-187n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "187N Review of operation of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security\nmust review the operation of this Part.\n\n(1A) The review:\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nData retention  Part 5-1A\nMiscellaneous  Division 4\n\nSection 187P\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) must start on or before the second anniversary of the end of\nthe implementation phase; and\n\n(b) must be concluded on or before the third anniversary of the\nend of the implementation phase.\n\n(2) The Committee must give the Minister a written report of the\nreview.\n\n(3) Until the review is completed, the head (however described) of an\nenforcement agency must keep:\n\n(a) all of the documents that he or she is required to retain under\nsection 185; and\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 186(1)(e) to (k), to include in a report under\nsubsection 186(1);\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(4) Until the review is completed, the Director-General of Security\nmust keep:\n\n(a) all of the authorisations made under Division 3 of Part 4-1;\nand\n\n(b) all of the information that he or she is required, by\nparagraphs 94(2A)(c) to (j) of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979, to include in a report\nreferred to in subsection 94(1) of that Act;\nrelating to the period starting on the commencement of this Part\nand ending when the review is completed.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not limit any other obligation to keep\ninformation under this Act or another law."
    },
    {
