    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-188",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "188 Delivery points",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-188"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each carrier must:\n\n(a) nominate, in respect of a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service of that carrier and in respect of\neach interception agency, at least one place in Australia as\nthe location of a point from which lawfully intercepted\ninformation can most conveniently be transmitted in relation\nto that interception agency; and\n\n(b) inform a Communications Access Coordinator of the place or\nplaces nominated for each interception agency.\nNote 1:\nThe nominated location becomes a delivery point: see the definition of\ndelivery point in subsection 5(1).\nNote 2:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\nNote 3:\nDelivery points are significant for the interception capability\nobligations in Part 5-3 and for the delivery capability obligations in",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each carrier must:\n\n(a) nominate, in respect of a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service of that carrier and in respect of\neach interception agency, at least one place in Australia as\nthe location of a point from which lawfully intercepted\ninformation can most conveniently be transmitted in relation\nto that interception agency; and\n\n(b) inform a Communications Access Coordinator of the place or\nplaces nominated for each interception agency.\nNote 1:\nThe nominated location becomes a delivery point: see the definition of\ndelivery point in subsection 5(1).\nNote 2:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\nNote 3:\nDelivery points are significant for the interception capability\nobligations in Part 5-3 and for the delivery capability obligations in",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-188-norm"
        },
