    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "189 Minister may make determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-189"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make determinations\nin relation to interception capabilities applicable to a specified kind\nof telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system.\n\n(2) A determination:\n\n(a) must specify an international standard or guidelines (the\ninternational standard), or the relevant part of the\ninternational standard, on which the determination is based;\nand\n\n(b) must provide for interception capability by adopting,\napplying or incorporating the whole or a part of the\ninternational standard, with only such modifications as are\nnecessary to facilitate the application of the standard or the\nrelevant part of the standard in Australia (including any\ntransitional arrangement in relation to an existing kind of\ntelecommunications service that might be required); and\n\n(c) must be accompanied by a copy of the international standard\nor of the relevant part of the international standard.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the international standard\nspecified in a determination:\n\n(a) must deal primarily with the requirements of interception\nagencies in relation to the interception of communications\npassing over a telecommunications network and related\nmatters; and\n\n(b) may be a part of an international agreement or arrangement\nor a proposed international agreement or arrangement.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability  Part 5-3\nObligations  Division 1\n\nSection 190\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMatters to be taken into account\n\n(4) Before making a determination under subsection (1), the Minister\nmust take into account:\n\n(a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and\n\n(b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the privacy of the users of telecommunications systems.\n\n(5) The Minister may take into account any other matter the Minister\nconsiders relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make determinations\nin relation to interception capabilities applicable to a specified kind\nof telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system.\n\n(2) A determination:\n\n(a) must specify an international standard or guidelines (the\ninternational standard), or the relevant part of the\ninternational standard, on which the determination is based;\nand\n\n(b) must provide for interception capability by adopting,\napplying or incorporating the whole or a part of the\ninternational standard, with only such modifications as are\nnecessary to facilitate the application of the standard or the\nrelevant part of the standard in Australia (including any\ntransitional arrangement in relation to an existing kind of\ntelecommunications service that might be required); and\n\n(c) must be accompanied by a copy of the international standard\nor of the relevant part of the international standard.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the international standard\nspecified in a determination:\n\n(a) must deal primarily with the requirements of interception\nagencies in relation to the interception of communications\npassing over a telecommunications network and related\nmatters; and\n\n(b) may be a part of an international agreement or arrangement\nor a proposed international agreement or arrangement.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability  Part 5-3\nObligations  Division 1\n\nSection 190\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMatters to be taken into account\n\n(4) Before making a determination under subsection (1), the Minister\nmust take into account:\n\n(a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and\n\n(b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the privacy of the users of telecommunications systems.\n\n(5) The Minister may take into account any other matter the Minister\nconsiders relevant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-189-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "008ef96d983ced837e5ebc3ac318566d9ebb642cdec236dfb48d8a136eac7896"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-189",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "189 Minister may make determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make determinations\nin relation to interception capabilities applicable to a specified kind\nof telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system.\n\n(2) A determination:\n\n(a) must specify an international standard or guidelines (the\ninternational standard), or the relevant part of the\ninternational standard, on which the determination is based;\nand\n\n(b) must provide for interception capability by adopting,\napplying or incorporating the whole or a part of the\ninternational standard, with only such modifications as are\nnecessary to facilitate the application of the standard or the\nrelevant part of the standard in Australia (including any\ntransitional arrangement in relation to an existing kind of\ntelecommunications service that might be required); and\n\n(c) must be accompanied by a copy of the international standard\nor of the relevant part of the international standard.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the international standard\nspecified in a determination:\n\n(a) must deal primarily with the requirements of interception\nagencies in relation to the interception of communications\npassing over a telecommunications network and related\nmatters; and\n\n(b) may be a part of an international agreement or arrangement\nor a proposed international agreement or arrangement.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability  Part 5-3\nObligations  Division 1\n\nSection 190\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMatters to be taken into account\n\n(4) Before making a determination under subsection (1), the Minister\nmust take into account:\n\n(a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and\n\n(b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(c) the privacy of the users of telecommunications systems.\n\n(5) The Minister may take into account any other matter the Minister\nconsiders relevant."
    },
