      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the international standard\nspecified in a determination:\n\n(a) must deal primarily with the requirements of interception\nagencies in relation to the interception of communications\npassing over a telecommunications network and related\nmatters; and\n\n(b) may be a part of an international agreement or arrangement\nor a proposed international agreement or arrangement.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability  Part 5-3\nObligations  Division 1\n\nSection 190\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMatters to be taken into account",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the international standard\nspecified in a determination:\n\n(a) must deal primarily with the requirements of interception\nagencies in relation to the interception of communications\npassing over a telecommunications network and related\nmatters; and\n\n(b) may be a part of an international agreement or arrangement\nor a proposed international agreement or arrangement.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability  Part 5-3\nObligations  Division 1\n\nSection 190\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMatters to be taken into account",
