    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "190(2) Obligations of persons covered by a determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-190-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ninterception capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote 1:\nA person may be exempted from the requirements of this section\nunder a provision of Division 2.\nNote 2:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2\nof Part 5-6.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ninterception capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote 1:\nA person may be exempted from the requirements of this section\nunder a provision of Division 2.\nNote 2:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2\nof Part 5-6.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
