        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3d9e968dc735c4884445ddb38c4480bd15cc92e2c50597f19f685ef43d4382d",
      "skos:note": "Carrier must ensure interception capability is developed, installed and maintained."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-190-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "190(2) Obligations of persons covered by a determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ninterception capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote 1:\nA person may be exempted from the requirements of this section\nunder a provision of Division 2.\nNote 2:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2\nof Part 5-6."
    },
