    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-192-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "192(5) Communications Access Coordinator may grant exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-192-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n\n(a) a person applies in writing to a Communications Access\nCoordinator for an exemption under subsection (1) from all\nthe obligations, or from particular obligations, imposed on\nthe person under Division 1 in so far as those obligations\nrelate to a specified kind of telecommunications service; and\n\n(b) a Communications Access Coordinator does not make, and\ncommunicate to the applicant, a decision granting, or\nrefusing to grant, the exemption within 60 days after the day\non which a Communications Access Coordinator receives the\napplication;\na Communications Access Coordinator is taken, at the end of that\nperiod of 60 days, to have granted an exemption to the applicant\nfrom the obligations to which the application relates in so far as\nthose obligations relate to that kind of telecommunications service.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If:\n\n(a) a person applies in writing to a Communications Access\nCoordinator for an exemption under subsection (1) from all\nthe obligations, or from particular obligations, imposed on\nthe person under Division 1 in so far as those obligations\nrelate to a specified kind of telecommunications service; and\n\n(b) a Communications Access Coordinator does not make, and\ncommunicate to the applicant, a decision granting, or\nrefusing to grant, the exemption within 60 days after the day\non which a Communications Access Coordinator receives the\napplication;\na Communications Access Coordinator is taken, at the end of that\nperiod of 60 days, to have granted an exemption to the applicant\nfrom the obligations to which the application relates in so far as\nthose obligations relate to that kind of telecommunications service.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-192"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-192-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f053ddd9660520a0090913634c9eafc8715d79a794411c4e6ed7b9cd31791e9a",
      "skos:note": "Granting exemption from obligations under Division 1 for a specified kind of telecommunications service."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-192-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "192(5) Communications Access Coordinator may grant exemptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n\n(a) a person applies in writing to a Communications Access\nCoordinator for an exemption under subsection (1) from all\nthe obligations, or from particular obligations, imposed on\nthe person under Division 1 in so far as those obligations\nrelate to a specified kind of telecommunications service; and\n\n(b) a Communications Access Coordinator does not make, and\ncommunicate to the applicant, a decision granting, or\nrefusing to grant, the exemption within 60 days after the day\non which a Communications Access Coordinator receives the\napplication;\na Communications Access Coordinator is taken, at the end of that\nperiod of 60 days, to have granted an exemption to the applicant\nfrom the obligations to which the application relates in so far as\nthose obligations relate to that kind of telecommunications service."
    },
