    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-195",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195 Nature of an interception capability plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-195"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An interception capability plan (IC plan) of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider is a written instrument that complies with\nsubsections (2) and (3).\nMatters to be included in the instrument\n\n(2) The instrument must set out:\n\n(a) a statement of the policies of the carrier or provider in\nrelation to interception generally and of its strategies for\ncompliance with its legal obligation to provide interception\ncapabilities in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system; and\n\n(b) a statement of the compliance by the carrier or provider with\nthat legal obligation; and\n\n(c) a statement of any relevant developments in the business of\nthe carrier or provider that are proposed within the period of\n5 years from the start of the plan and that, if implemented,\nare likely to affect those interception capabilities; and\n\n(d) a statement of the locations at which communications passing\nover a telecommunications system are intercepted or\nproposed to be intercepted by the carrier or provider; and\n\n(e) a list of employees of the carrier or provider with\nresponsibility for interception and other related matters; and\n\n(f) the matters determined by the Minister under subsection (4).\nApproval of instrument\n\n(3) The instrument must be approved by the chief executive officer\n(however described) of the carrier or provider or by a person\nauthorised in writing by that officer for the purposes of this\nsubsection to approve the instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An interception capability plan (IC plan) of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider is a written instrument that complies with\nsubsections (2) and (3).\nMatters to be included in the instrument\n\n(2) The instrument must set out:\n\n(a) a statement of the policies of the carrier or provider in\nrelation to interception generally and of its strategies for\ncompliance with its legal obligation to provide interception\ncapabilities in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system; and\n\n(b) a statement of the compliance by the carrier or provider with\nthat legal obligation; and\n\n(c) a statement of any relevant developments in the business of\nthe carrier or provider that are proposed within the period of\n5 years from the start of the plan and that, if implemented,\nare likely to affect those interception capabilities; and\n\n(d) a statement of the locations at which communications passing\nover a telecommunications system are intercepted or\nproposed to be intercepted by the carrier or provider; and\n\n(e) a list of employees of the carrier or provider with\nresponsibility for interception and other related matters; and\n\n(f) the matters determined by the Minister under subsection (4).\nApproval of instrument\n\n(3) The instrument must be approved by the chief executive officer\n(however described) of the carrier or provider or by a person\nauthorised in writing by that officer for the purposes of this\nsubsection to approve the instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-195-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-195-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-195-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "abfefabeb42e2d6bc2a22804d00920529ba876cb96a275846d8d314f5b8ff3dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-195",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195 Nature of an interception capability plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An interception capability plan (IC plan) of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider is a written instrument that complies with\nsubsections (2) and (3).\nMatters to be included in the instrument\n\n(2) The instrument must set out:\n\n(a) a statement of the policies of the carrier or provider in\nrelation to interception generally and of its strategies for\ncompliance with its legal obligation to provide interception\ncapabilities in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the\nuse of a telecommunications system; and\n\n(b) a statement of the compliance by the carrier or provider with\nthat legal obligation; and\n\n(c) a statement of any relevant developments in the business of\nthe carrier or provider that are proposed within the period of\n5 years from the start of the plan and that, if implemented,\nare likely to affect those interception capabilities; and\n\n(d) a statement of the locations at which communications passing\nover a telecommunications system are intercepted or\nproposed to be intercepted by the carrier or provider; and\n\n(e) a list of employees of the carrier or provider with\nresponsibility for interception and other related matters; and\n\n(f) the matters determined by the Minister under subsection (4).\nApproval of instrument\n\n(3) The instrument must be approved by the chief executive officer\n(however described) of the carrier or provider or by a person\nauthorised in writing by that officer for the purposes of this\nsubsection to approve the instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"
    },
