    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "196 Time for giving IC plans by carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-196"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A carrier must give an IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator by:\n\n(a) each 1 July; or\n\n(b) if a Communications Access Coordinator agrees to a later\nday instead of a particular 1 July—that later day.\nNote:\nIf the business plans of the carrier change, the carrier may be required\nto give a Communications Access Coordinator another IC plan under\nsection 201.\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator must inform the ACMA of\nany agreement under paragraph (1)(b).\nFurther rule for future carriers\n\n(3) If the carrier became a carrier on a day (the start day) after the\ncommencement of this section, the carrier must also give an IC\nplan to a Communications Access Coordinator within 90 days after\nthe start day.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A carrier must give an IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator by:\n\n(a) each 1 July; or\n\n(b) if a Communications Access Coordinator agrees to a later\nday instead of a particular 1 July—that later day.\nNote:\nIf the business plans of the carrier change, the carrier may be required\nto give a Communications Access Coordinator another IC plan under\nsection 201.\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator must inform the ACMA of\nany agreement under paragraph (1)(b).\nFurther rule for future carriers\n\n(3) If the carrier became a carrier on a day (the start day) after the\ncommencement of this section, the carrier must also give an IC\nplan to a Communications Access Coordinator within 90 days after\nthe start day.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf038c1e91586ffa07535855b9186b262460facd415c2c6027b3cfc0ac592058"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-196",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "196 Time for giving IC plans by carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A carrier must give an IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator by:\n\n(a) each 1 July; or\n\n(b) if a Communications Access Coordinator agrees to a later\nday instead of a particular 1 July—that later day.\nNote:\nIf the business plans of the carrier change, the carrier may be required\nto give a Communications Access Coordinator another IC plan under\nsection 201.\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator must inform the ACMA of\nany agreement under paragraph (1)(b).\nFurther rule for future carriers\n\n(3) If the carrier became a carrier on a day (the start day) after the\ncommencement of this section, the carrier must also give an IC\nplan to a Communications Access Coordinator within 90 days after\nthe start day."
    },
