    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-201",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "201 Consequences of changed business plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-201"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, because of changes to the business plans of a carrier or\nnominated carriage service provider, an IC plan given by that\ncarrier or provider ceases, during the period before another such IC\nplan is due to be given, to constitute an adequate IC plan of that\ncarrier or provider, the carrier or provider must:\n\n(a) prepare a new IC plan having regard to those changed\nbusiness plans; and\n\n(b) give the new IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThe new IC plan is subject to consideration in accordance with\nsection 198.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if the change in business plans has, or\nis likely to have, a material adverse effect on the ability of the\ncarrier or provider to comply with its obligations under Part 5-3.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability plans  Part 5-4\n\nSection 202\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, because of changes to the business plans of a carrier or\nnominated carriage service provider, an IC plan given by that\ncarrier or provider ceases, during the period before another such IC\nplan is due to be given, to constitute an adequate IC plan of that\ncarrier or provider, the carrier or provider must:\n\n(a) prepare a new IC plan having regard to those changed\nbusiness plans; and\n\n(b) give the new IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThe new IC plan is subject to consideration in accordance with\nsection 198.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if the change in business plans has, or\nis likely to have, a material adverse effect on the ability of the\ncarrier or provider to comply with its obligations under Part 5-3.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability plans  Part 5-4\n\nSection 202\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-201-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-201-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44b62661472741646978c496871126dd38d4ff47120a310321954a91d6405106"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-201",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "201 Consequences of changed business plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, because of changes to the business plans of a carrier or\nnominated carriage service provider, an IC plan given by that\ncarrier or provider ceases, during the period before another such IC\nplan is due to be given, to constitute an adequate IC plan of that\ncarrier or provider, the carrier or provider must:\n\n(a) prepare a new IC plan having regard to those changed\nbusiness plans; and\n\n(b) give the new IC plan to a Communications Access\nCoordinator as soon as practicable.\nNote:\nThe new IC plan is subject to consideration in accordance with\nsection 198.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies only if the change in business plans has, or\nis likely to have, a material adverse effect on the ability of the\ncarrier or provider to comply with its obligations under Part 5-3.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nInterception capability plans  Part 5-4\n\nSection 202\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
