      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Subsection (1) applies only if the change in business plans has, or is likely to have, a material adverse effect on the ability of the carrier or provider to comply with its obligations under Part 5-3."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-202",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "202 Confidential treatment of IC plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-202"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "Once a Communications Access Coordinator, the ACMA or an\ninterception agency receives an IC plan of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider, the Coordinator, the ACMA or the\ninterception agency:\n\n(a) must treat the plan as confidential; and\n\n(b) must ensure that it is not disclosed to any person or body not\nreferred to in this section without the written permission of\nthe carrier or provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "Once a Communications Access Coordinator, the ACMA or an\ninterception agency receives an IC plan of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider, the Coordinator, the ACMA or the\ninterception agency:\n\n(a) must treat the plan as confidential; and\n\n(b) must ensure that it is not disclosed to any person or body not\nreferred to in this section without the written permission of\nthe carrier or provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-202-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-202-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec4e5d470169eacb4b59d84915b9a1633297cbf4af9f97152a64915a1d948d1e",
      "skos:note": "Must treat IC plan as confidential and ensure it is not disclosed without written permission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-202",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "202 Confidential treatment of IC plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "Once a Communications Access Coordinator, the ACMA or an\ninterception agency receives an IC plan of a carrier or nominated\ncarriage service provider, the Coordinator, the ACMA or the\ninterception agency:\n\n(a) must treat the plan as confidential; and\n\n(b) must ensure that it is not disclosed to any person or body not\nreferred to in this section without the written permission of\nthe carrier or provider.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-202-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
