    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-203",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "203 Communications Access Coordinator may make determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-203"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by writing, make\ndeterminations in relation to delivery capabilities applicable in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a specified kind of telecommunications service that involves,\nor will involve, the use of a telecommunications system and\nthat is supplied by one or more specified carriers; and\n\n(b) one or more specified interception agencies.\nNote 1:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 33(3AB) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 3:\nA determination may make different provision with respect to\ndifferent matters or different classes of matters (see subsection 33(3A)\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) must relate to all or any of\nthe following:\n\n(a) the format in which lawfully intercepted information is to be\ndelivered to an interception agency from the delivery point in\nrespect of a kind of telecommunications service and of that\ninterception agency;\n\n(b) the place to which, and manner in which, that information is\nto be delivered;\n\n(c) any ancillary information that should accompany that\ninformation.\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nbefore a determination is made under subsection (1).\n\n(4) A determination made under subsection (1) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by writing, make\ndeterminations in relation to delivery capabilities applicable in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a specified kind of telecommunications service that involves,\nor will involve, the use of a telecommunications system and\nthat is supplied by one or more specified carriers; and\n\n(b) one or more specified interception agencies.\nNote 1:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 33(3AB) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 3:\nA determination may make different provision with respect to\ndifferent matters or different classes of matters (see subsection 33(3A)\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) must relate to all or any of\nthe following:\n\n(a) the format in which lawfully intercepted information is to be\ndelivered to an interception agency from the delivery point in\nrespect of a kind of telecommunications service and of that\ninterception agency;\n\n(b) the place to which, and manner in which, that information is\nto be delivered;\n\n(c) any ancillary information that should accompany that\ninformation.\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nbefore a determination is made under subsection (1).\n\n(4) A determination made under subsection (1) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-203-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-203-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-203-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-203-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d89120109bbcbe584ca0d5ff7e1041698a51a8eab5a4187f3b77afa61ae01ec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-203",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "203 Communications Access Coordinator may make determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by writing, make\ndeterminations in relation to delivery capabilities applicable in\nrelation to:\n\n(a) a specified kind of telecommunications service that involves,\nor will involve, the use of a telecommunications system and\nthat is supplied by one or more specified carriers; and\n\n(b) one or more specified interception agencies.\nNote 1:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 33(3AB) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 3:\nA determination may make different provision with respect to\ndifferent matters or different classes of matters (see subsection 33(3A)\nof the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) must relate to all or any of\nthe following:\n\n(a) the format in which lawfully intercepted information is to be\ndelivered to an interception agency from the delivery point in\nrespect of a kind of telecommunications service and of that\ninterception agency;\n\n(b) the place to which, and manner in which, that information is\nto be delivered;\n\n(c) any ancillary information that should accompany that\ninformation.\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nbefore a determination is made under subsection (1).\n\n(4) A determination made under subsection (1) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"
    },
