    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-204",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "204 Obligations of persons covered by a determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-204"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a determination under section 203 applies:\n\n(a) to a particular kind of telecommunications service that\ninvolves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications\nsystem; and\n\n(b) to a carrier;\nthe carrier must comply with the determination.\nNote:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ndelivery capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a determination under section 203 applies:\n\n(a) to a particular kind of telecommunications service that\ninvolves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications\nsystem; and\n\n(b) to a carrier;\nthe carrier must comply with the determination.\nNote:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ndelivery capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-204-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-204-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "520086be73ec53ef2b87532fe36a0e95644d0f6c435d7fb306899133f5f1d504"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-204",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "204 Obligations of persons covered by a determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a determination under section 203 applies:\n\n(a) to a particular kind of telecommunications service that\ninvolves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications\nsystem; and\n\n(b) to a carrier;\nthe carrier must comply with the determination.\nNote:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ndelivery capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6."
    },
