    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-204-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "204(2) Obligations of persons covered by a determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have\ndelivery capability in relation to a particular kind of\ntelecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is\nrequired to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and\nmaintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-204-ss-2-norm",
