    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-205",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "205 Obligations of persons not covered by a determination in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-205"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "relation to a kind of telecommunications service\n\n(1) Each carrier supplying a particular kind of telecommunications\nservice that is not covered by any determination under section 203\nbut that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications\nsystem must ensure that the kind of service or the system has a\ndelivery capability.\nNote:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the obligation under that\nsubsection includes the obligation to ensure that the capability is\ndeveloped, installed and maintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nAllocation of costs  Part 5-6\nOutline of Part  Division 1\n\nSection 206\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "relation to a kind of telecommunications service\n\n(1) Each carrier supplying a particular kind of telecommunications\nservice that is not covered by any determination under section 203\nbut that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications\nsystem must ensure that the kind of service or the system has a\ndelivery capability.\nNote:\nThe definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service\nproviders.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the obligation under that\nsubsection includes the obligation to ensure that the capability is\ndeveloped, installed and maintained.\nNote:\nThe cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies:\nsee Division 3 of Part 5-6.\n\nCo-operation with agencies  Chapter 5\nAllocation of costs  Part 5-6\nOutline of Part  Division 1\n\nSection 206\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
