      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Definition of carrier in subsection 5(1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-209",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "209 Working out costs of delivery capabilities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-209"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each carrier who is obliged to ensure the development, installation\nand maintenance of a delivery capability must ensure that the\ncapability is developed, installed and maintained on such terms and\nconditions:\n\n(a) as are agreed in writing between the carrier and the\ninterception agency concerned; or\n\n(b) in the absence of such an agreement—as are determined in\nwriting by the ACMA.\n\n(2) The terms and conditions on which a carrier is to provide a\ndelivery capability must be consistent with the following\nprinciples:\n\n(a) the principle that the most cost effective means of ensuring\nthe development, installation and maintenance of that\ncapability is employed;\n\n(b) the principle that the carrier is to incur the costs (whether of a\ncapital nature or otherwise) relating to the development,\ninstallation and maintenance of that capability;\n\n(c) the principle that the carrier may, over time, recover from an\ninterception agency such of those costs as are required, under\nsection 208, to be borne by that interception agency.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each carrier who is obliged to ensure the development, installation\nand maintenance of a delivery capability must ensure that the\ncapability is developed, installed and maintained on such terms and\nconditions:\n\n(a) as are agreed in writing between the carrier and the\ninterception agency concerned; or\n\n(b) in the absence of such an agreement—as are determined in\nwriting by the ACMA.\n\n(2) The terms and conditions on which a carrier is to provide a\ndelivery capability must be consistent with the following\nprinciples:\n\n(a) the principle that the most cost effective means of ensuring\nthe development, installation and maintenance of that\ncapability is employed;\n\n(b) the principle that the carrier is to incur the costs (whether of a\ncapital nature or otherwise) relating to the development,\ninstallation and maintenance of that capability;\n\n(c) the principle that the carrier may, over time, recover from an\ninterception agency such of those costs as are required, under\nsection 208, to be borne by that interception agency.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-209-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-209-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fd5cf78c5fe27dce2f4e753a024619b09004689f5bd655cee1510bc0591dbb8b"
    },
