    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-210",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "210 Examination of lower cost options",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-210"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may on\nits own initiative or at the request of an interception agency, by\nnotice in writing given to a carrier, require the carrier:\n\n(a) to examine, at the expense of the carrier, the possibility of a\nlower cost option than the one designated by the carrier for\nproviding a delivery capability; and\n\n(b) to report to the ACMA, within a period specified in the\nnotice, on the results of that examination.\n\n(2) If a carrier receives a notice under subsection (1), the carrier must,\nwithin the period specified in the notice:\n\n(a) carry out the examination concerned; and\n\n(b) report in writing to the ACMA on the results of the\nexamination.\n\n(3) A notice given under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may on\nits own initiative or at the request of an interception agency, by\nnotice in writing given to a carrier, require the carrier:\n\n(a) to examine, at the expense of the carrier, the possibility of a\nlower cost option than the one designated by the carrier for\nproviding a delivery capability; and\n\n(b) to report to the ACMA, within a period specified in the\nnotice, on the results of that examination.\n\n(2) If a carrier receives a notice under subsection (1), the carrier must,\nwithin the period specified in the notice:\n\n(a) carry out the examination concerned; and\n\n(b) report in writing to the ACMA on the results of the\nexamination.\n\n(3) A notice given under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-210-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-210-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-210-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "465f3e4848df3d2d6e032952b6cb0047576fde0c1060731dd090259ae35f154d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-210",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "210 Examination of lower cost options",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may on\nits own initiative or at the request of an interception agency, by\nnotice in writing given to a carrier, require the carrier:\n\n(a) to examine, at the expense of the carrier, the possibility of a\nlower cost option than the one designated by the carrier for\nproviding a delivery capability; and\n\n(b) to report to the ACMA, within a period specified in the\nnotice, on the results of that examination.\n\n(2) If a carrier receives a notice under subsection (1), the carrier must,\nwithin the period specified in the notice:\n\n(a) carry out the examination concerned; and\n\n(b) report in writing to the ACMA on the results of the\nexamination.\n\n(3) A notice given under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
