      "cml:integrityHash": "85d3b270a804462313a49e1aee0d2f6ec69a76e2ebbb8d529cd234eb7a31f1bf",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may require carrier to examine lower cost options and report results.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-210-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "210(1) Examination of lower cost options",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may on\nits own initiative or at the request of an interception agency, by\nnotice in writing given to a carrier, require the carrier:\n\n(a) to examine, at the expense of the carrier, the possibility of a\nlower cost option than the one designated by the carrier for\nproviding a delivery capability; and\n\n(b) to report to the ACMA, within a period specified in the\nnotice, on the results of that examination."
    },
    {
