    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-211",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "211 ACMA may require independent audit of costs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-211"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may,\nby notice in writing, require a carrier to arrange for an audit of the\ncosts claimed to have been incurred by the carrier in relation to the\nprovision to an interception agency of a delivery capability.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the audit is to be carried out by an\nauditor selected by the carrier and approved by the ACMA.\n\n(3) If the auditor selected by a carrier is not approved by the ACMA,\nthe ACMA may require that the audit be carried out by an auditor\nselected by the ACMA or by the ACMA itself.\n\n(4) Unless the audit is carried out by the ACMA itself, the ACMA\nmay, in the notice requiring the audit, specify the period within\nwhich the auditor is to report to the ACMA.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may,\nby notice in writing, require a carrier to arrange for an audit of the\ncosts claimed to have been incurred by the carrier in relation to the\nprovision to an interception agency of a delivery capability.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the audit is to be carried out by an\nauditor selected by the carrier and approved by the ACMA.\n\n(3) If the auditor selected by a carrier is not approved by the ACMA,\nthe ACMA may require that the audit be carried out by an auditor\nselected by the ACMA or by the ACMA itself.\n\n(4) Unless the audit is carried out by the ACMA itself, the ACMA\nmay, in the notice requiring the audit, specify the period within\nwhich the auditor is to report to the ACMA.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-211-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-211-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-211-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-211-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "95fe06c50af425394686f750d83a9a61601947337645c1cacbd93ec86af3c321"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-211",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "211 ACMA may require independent audit of costs",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In undertaking an arbitration under section 209, the ACMA may,\nby notice in writing, require a carrier to arrange for an audit of the\ncosts claimed to have been incurred by the carrier in relation to the\nprovision to an interception agency of a delivery capability.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the audit is to be carried out by an\nauditor selected by the carrier and approved by the ACMA.\n\n(3) If the auditor selected by a carrier is not approved by the ACMA,\nthe ACMA may require that the audit be carried out by an auditor\nselected by the ACMA or by the ACMA itself.\n\n(4) Unless the audit is carried out by the ACMA itself, the ACMA\nmay, in the notice requiring the audit, specify the period within\nwhich the auditor is to report to the ACMA.\n\nChapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"
    },
