    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits setting out English text of agreement in regulations.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If there is an agreement between Australia and a foreign country...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...a copy of the English text of the agreement must not be set out in regulations..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines temporal interval for obtaining information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "For the purposes of this subclause, information is obtained by virtue of the agreement if it is obtained in accordance with such an order.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...in connection with any proceeding by way of a prosecution for a death penalty offence..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-2-logic-diffusion-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuse",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Diffuses information about Australian-sourced information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "For Australian-sourced information, see subclause (8).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...in connection with any proceeding by way of a prosecution for a death penalty offence..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-2-logic-cogai-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognize",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recognizes the importance of written assurance from foreign country's government.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Note 2: For death penalty offence, see subclause (7A).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...unless the Minister has received a written assurance..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-2-logic-shacl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:SHACL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Validate",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Validates the content of regulations.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::shacl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If there is an agreement between Australia and a foreign country...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the issue of orders (however described) by a competent authority..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3(3) Designated international agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, if:\n\n(a) there is an agreement between Australia and 2 or more\nforeign countries; and\n\n(b) a copy of the English text of the agreement is set out in the\nregulations; and\n\n(c) the agreement has entered into force for Australia;\nthen:\n\n(d) if the agreement is affected by an amendment, where:\n\n(i) a copy of the English text of the amendment is set out in\nthe regulations; and\n\n(ii) the amendment has entered into force for Australia;\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, if:\n\n(a) there is an agreement between Australia and 2 or more\nforeign countries; and\n\n(b) a copy of the English text of the agreement is set out in the\nregulations; and\n\n(c) the agreement has entered into force for Australia;\nthen:\n\n(d) if the agreement is affected by an amendment, where:\n\n(i) a copy of the English text of the amendment is set out in\nthe regulations; and\n\n(ii) the amendment has entered into force for Australia;\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c74370f7aa329560290265eb9579227a4b9f8cc54da0826291021c6cdeb2fa05",
      "skos:note": "Conditional commencement based on agreement entering into force for Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3(3) Designated international agreement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, if:\n\n(a) there is an agreement between Australia and 2 or more\nforeign countries; and\n\n(b) a copy of the English text of the agreement is set out in the\nregulations; and\n\n(c) the agreement has entered into force for Australia;\nthen:\n\n(d) if the agreement is affected by an amendment, where:\n\n(i) a copy of the English text of the amendment is set out in\nthe regulations; and\n\n(ii) the amendment has entered into force for Australia;\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
