      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3A Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "agreements\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies to regulations made for the purposes of\nclause 3.\nDisallowance\n\n(2) Either House of the Parliament may, following a motion upon\nnotice, pass a resolution disallowing the regulations. For the\nresolution to be effective:\n\n(a) the notice must be given in that House within 15 sitting days\nof that House after the copy of the regulations was tabled in\nthat House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) the resolution must be passed, in pursuance of the motion,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that\nnotice.\n\n(3) If neither House passes such a resolution, the regulations takes\neffect on the day immediately after the last day upon which such a\nresolution could have been passed if it were assumed that notice of\na motion to disallow the regulations was given in each House on\nthe last day of the 15 sitting day period of that House mentioned in\nparagraph (2)(a).\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations.\n\n(5) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to the regulations.\nNote 1:\nThe 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this\nclause is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in\nparagraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003.\nNote 2:\nThe 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b)\nof this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period\nmentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003.",
      "skos:definition": "agreements\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies to regulations made for the purposes of\nclause 3.\nDisallowance\n\n(2) Either House of the Parliament may, following a motion upon\nnotice, pass a resolution disallowing the regulations. For the\nresolution to be effective:\n\n(a) the notice must be given in that House within 15 sitting days\nof that House after the copy of the regulations was tabled in\nthat House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) the resolution must be passed, in pursuance of the motion,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that\nnotice.\n\n(3) If neither House passes such a resolution, the regulations takes\neffect on the day immediately after the last day upon which such a\nresolution could have been passed if it were assumed that notice of\na motion to disallow the regulations was given in each House on\nthe last day of the 15 sitting day period of that House mentioned in\nparagraph (2)(a).\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations.\n\n(5) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to the regulations.\nNote 1:\nThe 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this\nclause is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in\npar",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b40ff257046ad69c4b6fc0e32647f7170a14b08f48c45643cf5e88dc2d7353cf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3A Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "agreements\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies to regulations made for the purposes of\nclause 3.\nDisallowance\n\n(2) Either House of the Parliament may, following a motion upon\nnotice, pass a resolution disallowing the regulations. For the\nresolution to be effective:\n\n(a) the notice must be given in that House within 15 sitting days\nof that House after the copy of the regulations was tabled in\nthat House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) the resolution must be passed, in pursuance of the motion,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that\nnotice.\n\n(3) If neither House passes such a resolution, the regulations takes\neffect on the day immediately after the last day upon which such a\nresolution could have been passed if it were assumed that notice of\na motion to disallow the regulations was given in each House on\nthe last day of the 15 sitting day period of that House mentioned in\nparagraph (2)(a).\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations.\n\n(5) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to the regulations.\nNote 1:\nThe 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this\nclause is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in\nparagraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003.\nNote 2:\nThe 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b)\nof this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period\nmentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003."
    },
