    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3A(4) Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "81c9b9d123e73305c668e12632e12a87b68b9731354487c4de57f3f3447f189c",
      "skos:note": "Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-3a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3A(4) Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 3B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nafter the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House\nunder section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and\n\n(b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of\nthat notice of motion:\n\n(i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has\nnot been called on; or\n\n(ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where\nrelevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or\notherwise disposed of;\nthe regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and\nsubclause (3) does not apply to the regulations."
    },
