    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Message application service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages\nto or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\nExample: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive\nemails from, any email address.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person provides a\nbilling service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message\napplication service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages\nto or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\nExample: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive\nemails from, any email address.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person provides a\nbilling service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message\napplication service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-4-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-4-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed5986c7851f7ba1c2a3cd34429f25a1eb84fe5ce6ca160e6498c4d0c41d1487"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Message application service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages\nto or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\nExample: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive\nemails from, any email address.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person provides a\nbilling service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message\napplication service."
    },
