    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 General electronic content service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, general electronic content\nservice means:\n\n(a) a service that allows end-users to access material using a\ntransmission service; or\n\n(b) a service that delivers material to persons having equipment\nappropriate for receiving that material, where the delivery of\nthe service is by means of a transmission service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(c) a message/call application service; or\n\n(d) a storage/back-up service; or\n\n(e) a service prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nsupplies a transmission service that enables material to be accessed\nor delivered.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nprovides a billing service, or a fee collection service, in relation to\na general electronic content service.\n9  When material is posted on a general electronic content service\n\nFor the purposes of this Schedule, material is posted on a general\nelectronic content service by a person if:\n\n(a) the person is an end-user of the service; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 10\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person causes the material to be accessible to, or\ndelivered to, one or more other end-users using the service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, general electronic content\nservice means:\n\n(a) a service that allows end-users to access material using a\ntransmission service; or\n\n(b) a service that delivers material to persons having equipment\nappropriate for receiving that material, where the delivery of\nthe service is by means of a transmission service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(c) a message/call application service; or\n\n(d) a storage/back-up service; or\n\n(e) a service prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nsupplies a transmission service that enables material to be accessed\nor delivered.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nprovides a billing service, or a fee collection service, in relation to\na general electronic content service.\n9  When material is posted on a general electronic content service\n\nFor the purposes of this Schedule, material is posted on a general\nelectronic content service by a person if:\n\n(a) the person is an end-user of the service; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 10\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person causes the material to be accessible to, or\ndelivered to, one or more other end-users using the service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-8-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-8-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-8-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "161da26c55a89b52a00d054701ee4677fa9bfd554ed5207f4957f132605b8c88"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 General electronic content service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, general electronic content\nservice means:\n\n(a) a service that allows end-users to access material using a\ntransmission service; or\n\n(b) a service that delivers material to persons having equipment\nappropriate for receiving that material, where the delivery of\nthe service is by means of a transmission service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(c) a message/call application service; or\n\n(d) a storage/back-up service; or\n\n(e) a service prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nsupplies a transmission service that enables material to be accessed\nor delivered.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\ngeneral electronic content service merely because the person\nprovides a billing service, or a fee collection service, in relation to\na general electronic content service.\n9  When material is posted on a general electronic content service\n\nFor the purposes of this Schedule, material is posted on a general\nelectronic content service by a person if:\n\n(a) the person is an end-user of the service; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 10\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person causes the material to be accessible to, or\ndelivered to, one or more other end-users using the service."
    },
