    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Identification of a particular person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Schedule, a particular person may be\nidentified:\n\n(a) by the person’s full name; or\n\n(b) by a name by which the person is commonly known; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 14\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) as the person to whom a particular individual transmission\nservice is supplied; or\n\n(d) as the person to whom a particular individual message/call\napplication service is provided; or\n\n(e) as the person who has a particular account with a prescribed\ncommunications provider; or\n\n(f) as the person who has a particular telephone number; or\n\n(g) as the person who has a particular email address; or\n\n(h) as the person who has a particular internet protocol address;\nor\n\n(i) as the person who has a device that has a particular unique\nidentifier (for example, an electronic serial number or a\nMedia Access Control address); or\n\n(j) by any other unique identifying factor that is applicable to the\nperson.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Schedule, a particular person may be\nidentified:\n\n(a) by the person’s full name; or\n\n(b) by a name by which the person is commonly known; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 14\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) as the person to whom a particular individual transmission\nservice is supplied; or\n\n(d) as the person to whom a particular individual message/call\napplication service is provided; or\n\n(e) as the person who has a particular account with a prescribed\ncommunications provider; or\n\n(f) as the person who has a particular telephone number; or\n\n(g) as the person who has a particular email address; or\n\n(h) as the person who has a particular internet protocol address;\nor\n\n(i) as the person who has a device that has a particular unique\nidentifier (for example, an electronic serial number or a\nMedia Access Control address); or\n\n(j) by any other unique identifying factor that is applicable to the\nperson.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-13-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f33013da6891cea18e7dd8a365e6037e63d576963c9188c4cf16d0c8e60aef43",
      "skos:note": "A particular person may be identified by various means."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 Identification of a particular person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 92,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Schedule, a particular person may be\nidentified:\n\n(a) by the person’s full name; or\n\n(b) by a name by which the person is commonly known; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 14\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) as the person to whom a particular individual transmission\nservice is supplied; or\n\n(d) as the person to whom a particular individual message/call\napplication service is provided; or\n\n(e) as the person who has a particular account with a prescribed\ncommunications provider; or\n\n(f) as the person who has a particular telephone number; or\n\n(g) as the person who has a particular email address; or\n\n(h) as the person who has a particular internet protocol address;\nor\n\n(i) as the person who has a device that has a particular unique\nidentifier (for example, an electronic serial number or a\nMedia Access Control address); or\n\n(j) by any other unique identifying factor that is applicable to the\nperson."
    },
