    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Eligible judge",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a person:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a\ndeclaration under subclause (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to an international production order applied for by\nthe National Anti-Corruption Commission—who is a\nsuperior Court Judge.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a person:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a\ndeclaration under subclause (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to an international production order applied for by\nthe National Anti-Corruption Commission—who is a\nsuperior Court Judge.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "426a901ee39dd821a6c4eb1d26098deb28f4253b64b21f564b0dc79f02ffbdc7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Eligible judge",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a person:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a\ndeclaration under subclause (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to an international production order applied for by\nthe National Anti-Corruption Commission—who is a\nsuperior Court Judge.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
