    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Issuing authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(ii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) is in\nforce; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 17\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years.\n\n(2) A person who is:\n\n(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(b) a magistrate;\nmay, by writing, consent to be appointed by the Attorney-General\nunder subclause (1).\n\n(3) A person’s appointment ceases to have effect if the person ceases\nto be a person whom the Attorney-General could appoint under this\nclause.\n\n(4) An appointment under subclause (1) has no effect for the purposes\nof a provision of this Act (other than this Schedule).\n\n(5) An issuing authority has, in relation to the performance or exercise\nof a function or power conferred on an issuing authority by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(ii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) is in\nforce; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 17\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years.\n\n(2) A person who is:\n\n(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(b) a magistrate;\nmay, by writing, consent to be appointed by the Attorney-General\nunder subclause (1).\n\n(3) A person’s appointment ceases to have effect if the person ceases\nto be a person whom the Attorney-General could appoint under this\nclause.\n\n(4) An appointment under subclause (1) has no effect for the purposes\nof a provision of this Act (other than this Schedule).\n\n(5) An issuing authority has, in relation to the performance or exercise\nof a function or power conferred on an issuing authority by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-16-ss-1"
        },
