    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-16-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16(1) Issuing authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(ii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) is in\nforce; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nIntroduction  Part 1\n\nClause 17\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years."
    },
