      "cml:premiseText": "Paragraph 51(v) (communications) of the Constitution",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Obligation to rely"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8372fb2a0339a01f7666d83a4691829e217ff5b6dd8f3e365c6fcf7122734364",
      "skos:note": "International production orders may be issued for serious offence investigation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-21-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ISSUE",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Issuing international production orders is obligatory",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply for an international production\norder under clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(1A) The interception agency may apply for the order to:\n\n(a) for an application made by the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission—an eligible Judge; or\n\n(b) otherwise—an eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n(i) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) a National Anti-Corruption Deputy Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the NACC who is authorised in\nwriting by the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner\nfor the purposes of this paragraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply for an international production\norder under clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(1A) The interception agency may apply for the order to:\n\n(a) for an application made by the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission—an eligible Judge; or\n\n(b) otherwise—an eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n(i) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) a National Anti-Corruption Deputy Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the NACC who is authorised in\nwriting by the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner\nfor the purposes of this paragraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-22-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-22-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-22-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-22-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89a1420b145908bae01e953e6f597567f43eb5d11b77ff56043c7b3042a442dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply for an international production\norder under clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(1A) The interception agency may apply for the order to:\n\n(a) for an application made by the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission—an eligible Judge; or\n\n(b) otherwise—an eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n(i) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) a National Anti-Corruption Deputy Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the NACC who is authorised in\nwriting by the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner\nfor the purposes of this paragraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
