      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
