      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "A written application under clause 22 by an interception agency for\nan international production order must set out:\n\n(a) the name of the agency; and\n\n(b) the name of the person making the application on the\nagency’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "A written application under clause 22 by an interception agency for\nan international production order must set out:\n\n(a) the name of the agency; and\n\n(b) the name of the person making the application on the\nagency’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
