      "values:originalText": "(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated ART member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated ART member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to interception: enforcement of the criminal law",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated ART member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated ART member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to interception: enforcement of the criminal law",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-28-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-28-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db8ea11efe8c3e2abde50ea0d733c3d5a11a505f04caa091104d366682611b81",
      "skos:note": "The Victorian PIM may question the person making the application or a required person in the presence of the eligible Judge or nominated ART member."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-28-ss-3",
