    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Application by interception agency of Queensland",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under clause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for an international production order under clause 30 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in subparagraphs 30(5)(a)(i)\nto (vi);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in\nsubparagraphs 30(5)(b)(i) to (vi).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Queensland PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated ART member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated ART member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Queensland PIM may only do so in the presence of\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under clause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for an international production order under clause 30 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in subparagraphs 30(5)(a)(i)\nto (vi);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in\nsubparagraphs 30(5)(b)(i) to (vi).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Queensland PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated ART member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated ART member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Queensland PIM may only do so in the presence of\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Application by interception agency of Queensland",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 107,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under clause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for an international production order under clause 30 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in subparagraphs 30(5)(a)(i)\nto (vi);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in\nsubparagraphs 30(5)(b)(i) to (vi).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Queensland PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated ART member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated ART member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Queensland PIM may only do so in the presence of\nthe eligible Judge or nominated ART member.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
