    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Issue of international production order—enforcement of the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "criminal law\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if an interception agency applies, under\nclause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART member for an\ninternational production order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the eligible Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated\nART member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:\n\n(i) the prescribed communications provider owns or\noperates a telecommunications network that is, or is\nlikely to be, used to supply those individual\ntransmission services; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to interception: enforcement of the criminal law",
      "skos:definition": "criminal law\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if an interception agency applies, under\nclause 22, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART member for an\ninternational production order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the eligible Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated\nART member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:\n\n(i) the prescribed communications provider owns or\noperates a telecommunications network that is, or is\nlikely to be, used to supply those individual\ntransmission services; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to interception: enforcement of the criminal law",
      "cml:hasPart": [
