      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder clause 33 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder clause 33 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "values:partOf": {
