    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Affidavits to accompany written application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, be\naccompanied by an affidavit complying with this clause.\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subclause (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, apart\nfrom this subclause, this clause would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 37\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, be\naccompanied by an affidavit complying with this clause.\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subclause (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, apart\nfrom this subclause, this clause would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 37\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-36-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-36-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-36-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f36c070eddb7161d1a2970e1f74c92104ce085e2852a00ddfb720ab283405710"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Affidavits to accompany written application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, be\naccompanied by an affidavit complying with this clause.\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subclause (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, apart\nfrom this subclause, this clause would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 37\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
