    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-40-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40(5) Content of international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-40-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency directly; or\n\n(b) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency indirectly\nvia the Australian Designated Authority.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 41\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency directly; or\n\n(b) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency indirectly\nvia the Australian Designated Authority.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 41\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-40"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-40-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19a95fd2fbc8a19909093b1da702304c9e73e4361a39fc9a54ba6d469b312b95",
      "skos:note": "Requirement for storing communications with criminal law-enforcement agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-40-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40(5) Content of international production order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 126,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency directly; or\n\n(b) require that a copy of stored communications be made\navailable to the criminal law-enforcement agency indirectly\nvia the Australian Designated Authority.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the\ncriminal law  Division 3\n\nClause 41\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
