      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to a\nperson, an international production order may be issued for\npurposes in connection with the monitoring of the person, so\nas to achieve a Part 5.3 object.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency, the agency must\nnotify the international production order to the Ombudsman\n(if the agency is not the ACC), or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (if the agency is the ACC).\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nClause 51\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to a\nperson, an international production order may be issued for\npurposes in connection with the monitoring of the person, so\nas to achieve a Part 5.3 object.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency, the agency must\nnotify the international production order to the Ombudsman\n(if the agency is not the ACC), or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (if the agency is the ACC).\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nClause 51\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-51-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb0ae257ca585e20936a37c1caebb804752a1c924469b2f4c7b4735541d03220",
      "skos:note": "International production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to a\nperson, an international production order may be issued for\npurposes in connection with the monitoring of the person, so\nas to achieve a Part 5.3 object.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a Part 5.3 IPO agency, the agency must\nnotify the international production order to the Ombudsman\n(if the agency is not the ACC), or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (if the agency is the ACC).\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nClause 51\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-51-norm",
