    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order on a Part 5.3 IPO agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 52 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order on a Part 5.3 IPO agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 52 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-53-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-53-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "532dde9753f530398b04267e41e5317c205016f008daf3aae61b6cfdde9eb3d8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Form of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 52 for an\ninternational production order on a Part 5.3 IPO agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 52 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf."
    },
