      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Issue of international production order—Part 5.3 supervisory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "order\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a Part 5.3 IPO agency applies, under\nclause 52, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART member for an\ninternational production order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the eligible Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated\nART member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:\n\n(i) the prescribed communications provider owns or\noperates a telecommunications network that is, or is\nlikely to be, used to supply those individual\ntransmission services; or\n\n(ii) the prescribed communications provider supplies those\nindividual transmission services; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that the prescribed communications provider\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to interception: Part 5.3 supervisory orders",
      "skos:definition": "order\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a Part 5.3 IPO agency applies, under\nclause 52, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART member for an\ninternational production order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the eligible Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the eligible Judge or nominated\nART member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that:\n\n(i) the prescribed communications provider owns or\noperates a telecommunications network that is, or is\nlikely to be, used to supply those individual\ntransmission services; or\n\n(ii) the prescribed communications provider supplies those\nindividual transmission services; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that the prescribed communications provider\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to interception: Part 5.3 supervisory orders",
