    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-62",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 Issue of further international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-62"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\ntransmission services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(k)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\nmessage/call application services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(l)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: Part 5.3 supervisory\norders  Division 3\n\nClause 63\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\ntransmission services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(k)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\nmessage/call application services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(l)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: Part 5.3 supervisory\norders  Division 3\n\nClause 63\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-62-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-62-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "994564c0a609c9b2e256c80ecb1a90baf5641b51833393605db158fdce217a8d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Issue of further international production order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\ntransmission services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(k)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 60; and\n\n(b) the original order was in respect of one or more individual\nmessage/call application services; and\n\n(c) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 60 that is:\n\n(d) in respect of any or all of those services; and\n\n(e) directed to the provider;\nso long as the period specified in the further order for the purposes\nof subparagraph 60(2)(l)(i) of this Schedule begins after the end of\nthe period specified in the original order for the purposes of that\nsubparagraph.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: Part 5.3 supervisory\norders  Division 3\n\nClause 63\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
