    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-70-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70(3) Content of international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-70-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The order must set out the following:\n\n(a) the date on which the order was issued;\n\n(b) the name of the Part 5.3 IPO agency;\n\n(c) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed;\n\n(d) the name of the designated international agreement\nnominated in the application for the order;\n\n(e) a statement to the effect that the order is issued on the basis\nof a Part 5.3 supervisory order made in relation to a person;\n\n(f) the name of the person;\n\n(g) a statement to the effect that the Part 5.3 supervisory order is:\n\n(i) an interim control order; or\n\n(ii) a confirmed control order; or\n\n(iii) an interim supervision order; or\n\n(iv) an extended supervision order.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: Part 5.3 supervisory\norders  Division 3\n\nClause 71\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The order must set out the following:\n\n(a) the date on which the order was issued;\n\n(b) the name of the Part 5.3 IPO agency;\n\n(c) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed;\n\n(d) the name of the designated international agreement\nnominated in the application for the order;\n\n(e) a statement to the effect that the order is issued on the basis\nof a Part 5.3 supervisory order made in relation to a person;\n\n(f) the name of the person;\n\n(g) a statement to the effect that the Part 5.3 supervisory order is:\n\n(i) an interim control order; or\n\n(ii) a confirmed control order; or\n\n(iii) an interim supervision order; or\n\n(iv) an extended supervision order.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nInternational production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3\nInternational production orders relating to stored communications: Part 5.3 supervisory\norders  Division 3\n\nClause 71\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-70"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
