    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-73-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73(2) Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-73-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.167",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a person making the application on the Part 5.3 IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, a person making the application on the Part 5.3 IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-73"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-73-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-73-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b7ed428fcb74b054b07bc9375620c60cd8a6d09b5f12b46a37ed00a648abcb9",
      "skos:note": "Telephone application permitted under urgent circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-73-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73(2) Form of application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 167,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a person making the application on the Part 5.3 IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
