    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "78 Issue of international production order—Part 5.3 supervisory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-78"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "order\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a Part 5.3 IPO agency applies, under\nclause 72, to an issuing authority for an international production\norder that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "order\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a Part 5.3 IPO agency applies, under\nclause 72, to an issuing authority for an international production\norder that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0c3933965d89cbceb8342c6b60dc0de12b88893cf57d4f88711874adeceac36a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-78",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "78 Issue of international production order—Part 5.3 supervisory",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "order\nScope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a Part 5.3 IPO agency applies, under\nclause 72, to an issuing authority for an international production\norder that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
