      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
