          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c14b15ee93ac650e9f8ef84edc7b1253b5addf1ffa494e2a099f04fb2d06d5e8",
      "skos:note": "Issue of international production order—Part 5.3 supervisory"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-78-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "78(2) Issue of international production order—Part 5.3 supervisory",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the issuing authority is satisfied, on the basis of the information\ngiven to the issuing authority under this Division in connection\nwith the application, that:\n\n(a) a Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force in relation to the\nrelevant person; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-78-ss-2-norm",
