      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-80-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The original order was issued before the further international production order.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "81 Notification to Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-81"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.175",
      "values:originalText": "Intelligence and Security by Part 5.3 IPO agencies in\nrelation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a Part 5.3 IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the order has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the order; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the\ncontravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "Intelligence and Security by Part 5.3 IPO agencies in\nrelation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a Part 5.3 IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the order has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the order; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the\ncontravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a44bf1448f62c4fe96600d9a38105fd33cc1b4c63eff44afc596c43ac6d75126"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-81",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "81 Notification to Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 175,
      "values:originalText": "Intelligence and Security by Part 5.3 IPO agencies in\nrelation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a Part 5.3 IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the order has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the order; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the\ncontravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
