      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.195",
      "values:originalText": "An application under clause 92 must, if it is in writing, set out:\n\n(a) a statement to the effect that the application is made by the\nOrganisation; and\n\n(b) the name of the person making the application on the\nOrganisation’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "An application under clause 92 must, if it is in writing, set out:\n\n(a) a statement to the effect that the application is made by the\nOrganisation; and\n\n(b) the name of the person making the application on the\nOrganisation’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:asserts": [
