      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c03087507db04ac4f57667581649a30982ab0f2553f54f721f154d2590663897",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on storing communications prejudicial to security"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-98-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "98(2) Issue of international production order—national security",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 197,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the nominated ART Intelligence and Security member is\nsatisfied, on the basis of the information given to the nominated\nART Intelligence and Security member under this Division in\nconnection with the application, that:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the relevant\nperson is engaged in, or is likely to engage in, activities\nprejudicial to security; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds any of the\nfollowing stored communications:\n\n(i) stored communications that consist of communications\nthat the relevant person has made using a\ntelecommunications network owned or operated by the\nprescribed communications provider;\n\n(ii) stored communications that consist of communications\nthat another person has made using a\ntelecommunications network owned or operated by the\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-98-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-98-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
