      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-110-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must consider if order complies with designated international agreement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Australian Designated Authority must consider whether the order complies with the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If the Australian Designated Authority is satisfied that the order complies with the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order, the Australian Designated Authority must give the order to the prescribed communications provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-110-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST NOT",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must cancel the order if it does not comply with designated international agreement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If the Australian Designated Authority is not satisfied that the order complies with the designated international agreement nominated in the application for the order, the Australian Designated Authority must cancel the order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-111",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "111 Giving of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-111"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.211",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an international production order is issued under Part 2 or 3 of\nthis Schedule:\n\n(a) the relevant agency that applied for the order must:\n\n(i) give the order, or a certified copy of the order, to the\nAustralian Designated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is issued; and\n\n(b) the Australian Designated Authority must consider whether\nthe order complies with the designated international\nagreement nominated in the application for the order; and\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an international production order is issued under Part 2 or 3 of\nthis Schedule:\n\n(a) the relevant agency that applied for the order must:\n\n(i) give the order, or a certified copy of the order, to the\nAustralian Designated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is issued; and\n\n(b) the Australian Designated Authority must consider whether\nthe order complies with the designated international\nagreement nominated in the application for the order; and\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-111-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-111-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f97499b07accb80d73f27d19a136dccb37d3efb96c7bfc4e1fd6b3f00c83897",
      "skos:note": "Agency must give order to Australian Designated Authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-111",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "111 Giving of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 211,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an international production order is issued under Part 2 or 3 of\nthis Schedule:\n\n(a) the relevant agency that applied for the order must:\n\n(i) give the order, or a certified copy of the order, to the\nAustralian Designated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is issued; and\n\n(b) the Australian Designated Authority must consider whether\nthe order complies with the designated international\nagreement nominated in the application for the order; and\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-111-norm",
