      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-112-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Organisation must give an international production order.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-113",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "113 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-113"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by the Organisation, the Director-General\nof Security:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the Director-General of\nSecurity is satisfied that the grounds on which the order\nwas issued have ceased to exist.\n•\nIf an international production order is revoked after it has\ncome into force, the Australian Designated Authority must\ngive the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider to whom the order is directed.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by the Organisation, the Director-General\nof Security:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the Director-General of\nSecurity is satisfied that the grounds on which the order\nwas issued have ceased to exist.\n•\nIf an international production order is revoked after it has\ncome into force, the Australian Designated Authority must\ngive the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider to whom the order is directed.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-113-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-113-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "455289c2408364ea87f0e00d3d60351157ac8c9bded97c3829d9b5d9e9de591d",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must revoke order if grounds cease to exist."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "113 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by the Organisation, the Director-General\nof Security:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the Director-General of\nSecurity is satisfied that the grounds on which the order\nwas issued have ceased to exist.\n•\nIf an international production order is revoked after it has\ncome into force, the Australian Designated Authority must\ngive the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider to whom the order is directed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-113-norm",
