    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-114",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "114 Revocation of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-114"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.216",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 115\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in force in\nrelation to a particular person when the international production\norder was issued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if,\nand only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor any\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 115\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in force in\nrelation to a particular person when the international production\norder was issued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if,\nand only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor any\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-114-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-114-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-114-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45f80ab8289085d333c2ebd67a8ec2c9695342c1649746ead71861ac0475db3a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-114",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "114 Revocation of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 216,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 115\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in force in\nrelation to a particular person when the international production\norder was issued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if,\nand only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor any\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force."
    },
