    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-115",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "115 Giving of instrument of revocation—relevant agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-115"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 114 by\nthe chief officer of a relevant agency, the relevant agency must:\n\n(a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 114;\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation\nis given to the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(3) A revocation under clause 114 takes effect:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 114 by\nthe chief officer of a relevant agency, the relevant agency must:\n\n(a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 114;\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation\nis given to the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(3) A revocation under clause 114 takes effect:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
