    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-116",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "116 Revocation of international production orders—the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-116"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "Organisation\n\n(1) If an international production order was issued under Part 4 of this\nSchedule, the Director-General of Security:\n\n(a) may revoke the order; and\n\n(b) must revoke the order if the Director-General of Security is\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the order was issued have\nceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Organisation\n\n(1) If an international production order was issued under Part 4 of this\nSchedule, the Director-General of Security:\n\n(a) may revoke the order; and\n\n(b) must revoke the order if the Director-General of Security is\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the order was issued have\nceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-116-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "350be3643ce78043f7c268bdcee1df0bd01bc04f4eb83a62beb66e76c6e776a7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-116",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "116 Revocation of international production orders—the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 218,
      "values:originalText": "Organisation\n\n(1) If an international production order was issued under Part 4 of this\nSchedule, the Director-General of Security:\n\n(a) may revoke the order; and\n\n(b) must revoke the order if the Director-General of Security is\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the order was issued have\nceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument."
    },
