    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "117 Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-117"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 116 by\nthe Director-General of Security, the Organisation must:\n\n(a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 118\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 116;\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation\nis given to the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(3) A revocation under clause 116 takes effect:\n\n(a) if the instrument of revocation is required to be given to the\nprescribed communications provider concerned—when the\ninstrument is given; or\n\n(b) otherwise—when the revocation is made.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under\nclause 116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 116 by\nthe Director-General of Security, the Organisation must:\n\n(a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 118\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 116;\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation\nis given to the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(3) A revocation under clause 116 takes effect:\n\n(a) if the instrument of revocation is required to be given to the\nprescribed communications provider concerned—when the\ninstrument is given; or\n\n(b) otherwise—when the revocation is made.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under\nclause 116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fd1729621342bd406acf68cf2d08fd6cc9f3dce53a6ce36705e545a3ccf3894a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-117",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "117 Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 218,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 116 by\nthe Director-General of Security, the Organisation must:\n\n(a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nRevocation of international production orders  Part 6\n\nClause 118\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 116;\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation\nis given to the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(3) A revocation under clause 116 takes effect:\n\n(a) if the instrument of revocation is required to be given to the\nprescribed communications provider concerned—when the\ninstrument is given; or\n\n(b) otherwise—when the revocation is made.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under\nclause 116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect."
    },
