    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122(3) Cancellation of international production orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-122-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If an international production order is cancelled under\nsubclause (1), the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(a) if the order was issued under Part 2 or 3 of this Schedule in\nresponse to an application by a relevant agency:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order;\nor\n\n(b) if the order was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If an international production order is cancelled under\nsubclause (1), the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(a) if the order was issued under Part 2 or 3 of this Schedule in\nresponse to an application by a relevant agency:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order;\nor\n\n(b) if the order was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a68d4c55870d6b1edc04f3e8ec964ce570f5f1729706ac3cf65d92026d52d258",
      "skos:note": "Inform relevant agencies or Organisation of cancellation",
      "dc:description": "Information about cancellation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-122-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122(3) Cancellation of international production orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If an international production order is cancelled under\nsubclause (1), the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(a) if the order was issued under Part 2 or 3 of this Schedule in\nresponse to an application by a relevant agency:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order;\nor\n\n(b) if the order was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order."
    },
    {
