    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122(4) Cancellation of international production orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-122-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (1);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of cancellation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (1);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of cancellation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4baf2d0e856b62ecaa3bd07198be22bd2190e24ecadf4177c11ef826371bd35c",
      "skos:note": "Must provide instrument of cancellation to prescribed communications provider after cancelling international production order.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-122-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122(4) Cancellation of international production orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (1);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(c) give the instrument of cancellation to the prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after cancelling the order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
