    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-130",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "130 Annual reports by the Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-130"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.230",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must, within 3 months after\nthe end of each financial year, give the Minister a written report\nthat sets out, for each relevant agency:\n\n(a) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were given by\nthe Australian Designated Authority to prescribed\ncommunications providers during the financial year:\n\n(i) the number of those orders; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement; and\n\n(b) if subparagraph 30(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 30 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 130\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) if subparagraph 60(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 60 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(d) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 111\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n\n(e) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 122\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n\n(f) if one or more instruments of revocation of international\nproduction orders issued in response to applications made by\nthe agency were given by the Australian Designated\nAuthority to prescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year—the number of those instruments; and\n\n(g) if one or more objections were received by the Australian\nDesignated Authority under clause 121 during the financial\nyear in relation to international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency:\n\n(i) the number of international production orders to which\nthose objections relate; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) cause a copy of a report under subclause (1) to be given to\nthe Attorney-General; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after receiving the report.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must, within 3 months after\nthe end of each financial year, give the Minister a written report\nthat sets out, for each relevant agency:\n\n(a) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were given by\nthe Australian Designated Authority to prescribed\ncommunications providers during the financial year:\n\n(i) the number of those orders; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement; and\n\n(b) if subparagraph 30(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 30 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 130\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) if subparagraph 60(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 60 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(d) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 111\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n\n(e) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 122\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-130-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-130-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ab6dbf409dd658120913050cb3611dbd60c43f36f9fed4389b8fdaee554aeac"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-130",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "130 Annual reports by the Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 230,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must, within 3 months after\nthe end of each financial year, give the Minister a written report\nthat sets out, for each relevant agency:\n\n(a) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were given by\nthe Australian Designated Authority to prescribed\ncommunications providers during the financial year:\n\n(i) the number of those orders; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement; and\n\n(b) if subparagraph 30(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 30 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 130\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) if subparagraph 60(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 60 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(d) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 111\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n\n(e) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\nby the Australian Designated Authority under clause 122\nduring the financial year—the number of those orders; and\n\n(f) if one or more instruments of revocation of international\nproduction orders issued in response to applications made by\nthe agency were given by the Australian Designated\nAuthority to prescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year—the number of those instruments; and\n\n(g) if one or more objections were received by the Australian\nDesignated Authority under clause 121 during the financial\nyear in relation to international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency:\n\n(i) the number of international production orders to which\nthose objections relate; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement.\n\n(2) The Minister must:\n\n(a) cause a copy of a report under subclause (1) to be given to\nthe Attorney-General; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after receiving the report.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
