    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "132 Deferral of inclusion of information in Ministerial report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-132"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.232",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to information:\n\n(a) included in a report given to the Minister:\n\n(i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant\nagency; or\n\n(ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 132\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to\ninclude in the next Ministerial report.\nExclusion of information—relevant agency\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the\ninformation is Part 5.3 information;\nthe chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include\nthe information in the next Ministerial report.\n\n(3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that\nthe information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:\n\n(a) notify the chief officer in writing; and\n\n(b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the\nMinister decides otherwise under subclause (5).\nInclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency\n\n(4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report\nbecause of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister\nprepares the next Ministerial report:\n\n(a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information;\nand\n\n(b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to information:\n\n(a) included in a report given to the Minister:\n\n(i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant\nagency; or\n\n(ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 132\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to\ninclude in the next Ministerial report.\nExclusion of information—relevant agency\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the\ninformation is Part 5.3 information;\nthe chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include\nthe information in the next Ministerial report.\n\n(3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that\nthe information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:\n\n(a) notify the chief officer in writing; and\n\n(b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the\nMinister decides otherwise under subclause (5).\nInclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency\n\n(4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report\nbecause of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister\nprepares the next Ministerial report:\n\n(a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information;\nand\n\n(b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-132",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "132 Deferral of inclusion of information in Ministerial report",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 232,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to information:\n\n(a) included in a report given to the Minister:\n\n(i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant\nagency; or\n\n(ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nReporting requirements  Division 2\n\nClause 132\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to\ninclude in the next Ministerial report.\nExclusion of information—relevant agency\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the\ninformation is Part 5.3 information;\nthe chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include\nthe information in the next Ministerial report.\n\n(3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that\nthe information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:\n\n(a) notify the chief officer in writing; and\n\n(b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the\nMinister decides otherwise under subclause (5).\nInclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency\n\n(4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report\nbecause of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister\nprepares the next Ministerial report:\n\n(a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information;\nand\n\n(b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-1",
