      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135(2) Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-135-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.240",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The period for which the Director-General of Security must cause a\ncopy of a particular document to be kept in the Organisation’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the document relates to an international production\norder that was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule; and\n\n(ii) information was obtained in accordance with the order;\n\nending at the later of the following times:\n\n(iii) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence;\n\n(iv) when the Organisation ceases to retain the information\nthat was obtained in accordance with the order; and\n\n(c) if paragraph (b) does not apply—ending when 3 years have\nelapsed since the document came into existence.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The period for which the Director-General of Security must cause a\ncopy of a particular document to be kept in the Organisation’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the document relates to an international production\norder that was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule; and\n\n(ii) information was obtained in accordance with the order;\n\nending at the later of the following times:\n\n(iii) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence;\n\n(iv) when the Organisation ceases to retain the information\nthat was obtained in accordance with the order; and\n\n(c) if paragraph (b) does not apply—ending when 3 years have\nelapsed since the document came into existence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4506234b7a9a7fc88c4f882253e864d798b99aa14ffa65f4bfba5bfaa903ea01",
      "skos:note": "The Organisation must keep a copy of the document for 3 years or until it ceases to retain information obtained in accordance with an international production order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-135-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135(2) Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 240,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The period for which the Director-General of Security must cause a\ncopy of a particular document to be kept in the Organisation’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the document relates to an international production\norder that was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule; and\n\n(ii) information was obtained in accordance with the order;\n\nending at the later of the following times:\n\n(iii) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence;\n\n(iv) when the Organisation ceases to retain the information\nthat was obtained in accordance with the order; and\n\n(c) if paragraph (b) does not apply—ending when 3 years have\nelapsed since the document came into existence."
    },
