    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-137",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137 Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-137"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.244",
      "values:originalText": "orders—Australian Designated Authority\n\n(1) The Australian Designated authority must cause the following to\nbe kept in the Australian Designated Authority’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each international production order given by the\nAustralian Designated Authority to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\n\n(b) if an instrument of revocation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of revocation;\n\n(c) if an instrument of cancellation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of cancellation;\n\n(d) a copy of each objection received by the Australian\nDesignated Authority under clause 121.\n\n(2) The period for which the Australian Designated Authority must\ncause a document to be kept in the Australian Designated\nAuthority’s records under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence.",
      "skos:definition": "orders—Australian Designated Authority\n\n(1) The Australian Designated authority must cause the following to\nbe kept in the Australian Designated Authority’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each international production order given by the\nAustralian Designated Authority to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\n\n(b) if an instrument of revocation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of revocation;\n\n(c) if an instrument of cancellation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of cancellation;\n\n(d) a copy of each objection received by the Australian\nDesignated Authority under clause 121.\n\n(2) The period for which the Australian Designated Authority must\ncause a document to be kept in the Australian Designated\nAuthority’s records under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-137-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-137-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "366326aa027c08b3d5383f264cbbdfac0769b41013861867234770a39c7be54b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-137",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137 Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 244,
      "values:originalText": "orders—Australian Designated Authority\n\n(1) The Australian Designated authority must cause the following to\nbe kept in the Australian Designated Authority’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each international production order given by the\nAustralian Designated Authority to a prescribed\ncommunications provider;\n\n(b) if an instrument of revocation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of revocation;\n\n(c) if an instrument of cancellation of an international production\norder was given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a copy of the\ninstrument of cancellation;\n\n(d) a copy of each objection received by the Australian\nDesignated Authority under clause 121.\n\n(2) The period for which the Australian Designated Authority must\ncause a document to be kept in the Australian Designated\nAuthority’s records under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence."
    },
