    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-138",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "138 Other records to be kept—Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-138"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.244",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must cause the following to\nbe kept in the Australian Designated Authority’s records:\n\n(a) for each international production order given by the\nAustralian Designated Authority to a prescribed\ncommunications provider:\n\n(i) a record of the type of order; and\n\n(ii) a record of the Australian entity that applied for the\norder; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nRecord-keeping requirements  Division 3\n\nClause 138\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iii) the name of the designated international agreement\ninvoked by the order; and\n\n(iv) the name of the prescribed communications provider;\nand\n\n(v) if, in compliance with the order, the prescribed\ncommunications provider made intercepted\ncommunications, messages, voice calls or video calls\navailable to an Australian entity directly—a statement to\nthat effect; and\n\n(vi) if, in compliance with the order, the prescribed\ncommunications provider made stored communications\nor telecommunications data available to an Australian\nentity directly—a statement to that effect;\n\n(b) if an international production order is cancelled by the\nAustralian Designated Authority under clause 111, 112 or\n122—a record of the cancellation and the reasons for the\ncancellation;\n\n(c) if an instrument of revocation of an international production\norder is given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a record of the giving\nof the instrument;\n\n(d) if an instrument of cancellation of an international production\norder is given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a record of the giving\nof the instrument;\n\n(e) if an objection is received by the Australian Designated\nAuthority under clause 121:\n\n(i) a record of the receipt of the objection; and\n\n(ii) a record of the international production order to which\nthe objection relates; and\n\n(iii) a record of the type of order; and\n\n(iv) the name of the designated international agreement\ninvoked by the order; and\n\n(v) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed; and\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must cause the following to\nbe kept in the Australian Designated Authority’s records:\n\n(a) for each international production order given by the\nAustralian Designated Authority to a prescribed\ncommunications provider:\n\n(i) a record of the type of order; and\n\n(ii) a record of the Australian entity that applied for the\norder; and\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nReporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9\nRecord-keeping requirements  Division 3\n\nClause 138\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iii) the name of the designated international agreement\ninvoked by the order; and\n\n(iv) the name of the prescribed communications provider;\nand\n\n(v) if, in compliance with the order, the prescribed\ncommunications provider made intercepted\ncommunications, messages, voice calls or video calls\navailable to an Australian entity directly—a statement to\nthat effect; and\n\n(vi) if, in compliance with the order, the prescribed\ncommunications provider made stored communications\nor telecommunications data available to an Australian\nentity directly—a statement to that effect;\n\n(b) if an international production order is cancelled by the\nAustralian Designated Authority under clause 111, 112 or\n122—a record of the cancellation and the reasons for the\ncancellation;\n\n(c) if an instrument of revocation of an international production\norder is given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a record of the giving\nof the instrument;\n\n(d) if an instrument of cancellation of an international production\norder is given by the Australian Designated Authority to a\nprescribed communications provider—a record of the giving\nof the instrument;\n\n(e) if an objection is received by the Australian Designated\nAuthority under clause 121:\n\n(i) a record of the receipt of the objection; and\n\n(ii) a record of the international production order to which\nthe objection relates; an",
