    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-148",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "148 Delegation by Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 260,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may, by writing, delegate:\n\n(a) to an APS employee responsible to the Ombudsman; or\n\n(b) to a person having similar oversight functions to the\nOmbudsman under the law of a State or Territory or to an\nemployee responsible to that person;\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Part 10\n\nClause 149\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nall or any of the Ombudsman’s powers under this Part other than a\npower to report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A delegate must, upon request by a person affected by the exercise\nof any power delegated to the delegate, produce the instrument of\ndelegation, or a copy of the instrument, for inspection by the\nperson."
    },
