      "cml:integrityHash": "774f2511b2ed334b45021addc0f39fc12aff2fda0eaac9384837017a5ad0a9ab",
      "skos:note": "Protected information may be used, recorded or disclosed for certain purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-158",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158 Exceptions—international production orders relating to stored",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 278,
      "values:originalText": "communications\n\nProtected information that:\n\n(a) was obtained in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 39, 69 or 98; or\n\n(b) relates to an international production order issued under\nclause 39, 69 or 98;\nmay be used, recorded or disclosed, or may be admitted in\nevidence, for any of the following purposes:\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nDisclosure of protected information  Part 11\n\nClause 159\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property in\nconnection with the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(d) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a serious category 1 offence;\n\n(e) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(f) a proceeding for recovery of a pecuniary penalty for a\ncontravention that would, if proved, render the person\ncommitting the contravention liable to:\n\n(i) a pecuniary penalty, or a maximum pecuniary penalty,\nof at least 60 penalty units if the contravention is\ncommitted by an individual; or\n\n(ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an\nindividual—a pecuniary penalty, or a maximum\npecuniary penalty, of at least 300 penalty units;\n\n(g) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003;\n\n(h) a police disciplinary proceeding."
    },
