    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "160 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-160"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.281",
      "values:originalText": "•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to comply with an\ninternational production order.\n•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to voluntarily\nprovide information in connection with an international\nproduction order.\n•\nA certifying officer of a relevant agency may issue an\nevidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to the\nreceipt by the agency of information that was made available\nto the agency in accordance with an international production\norder.\n•\nA certifying person may issue an evidentiary certificate setting\nout facts with respect to the receipt by the Organisation of\ninformation that was made available to the Organisation in\naccordance with an international production order.\n•\nIf an international production order requires information to be\nmade available to a relevant agency or the Organisation\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the\nAustralian Designated Authority may issue an evidentiary\ncertificate setting out facts with respect to:\n\n(a)\nthe receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ninformation; or\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to comply with an\ninternational production order.\n•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to voluntarily\nprovide information in connection with an international\nproduction order.\n•\nA certifying officer of a relevant agency may issue an\nevidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to the\nreceipt by the agency of information that was made available\nto the agency in accordance with an international production\norder.\n•\nA certifying person may issue an evidentiary certificate setting\nout facts with respect to the receipt by the Organisation of\ninformation that was made available to the Organisation in\naccordance with an international production order.\n•\nIf an international production order requires information to be\nmade available to a relevant agency or the Organisation\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the\nAustralian Designated Authority may issue an evidentiary\ncertificate setting out facts with respect to:\n\n(a)\nthe receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ninformation; or\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e46e65f680a35c0799bf0967e5661e3b6519af30cf5323519c610a18ed8efa1",
      "skos:note": "Issue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to acts or things done by the provider in order to comply with an international production order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-160",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "160 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 281,
      "values:originalText": "•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to comply with an\ninternational production order.\n•\nA manager of a prescribed communications provider may\nissue an evidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to\nacts or things done by the provider in order to voluntarily\nprovide information in connection with an international\nproduction order.\n•\nA certifying officer of a relevant agency may issue an\nevidentiary certificate setting out facts with respect to the\nreceipt by the agency of information that was made available\nto the agency in accordance with an international production\norder.\n•\nA certifying person may issue an evidentiary certificate setting\nout facts with respect to the receipt by the Organisation of\ninformation that was made available to the Organisation in\naccordance with an international production order.\n•\nIf an international production order requires information to be\nmade available to a relevant agency or the Organisation\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the\nAustralian Designated Authority may issue an evidentiary\ncertificate setting out facts with respect to:\n\n(a)\nthe receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ninformation; or\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-160-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Issue an evidentiary certificate",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-161",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "161 Evidentiary certificates—compliance with international",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-161"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.282",
      "values:originalText": "production orders by prescribed communications\nproviders\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is not an individual;\na manager of the provider may issue a written certificate signed by\nthe manager setting out such facts as the manager considers\nrelevant with respect to acts or things done by the provider in order\nto comply with the international production order.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is an individual;\nthe provider may issue a written certificate signed by the provider\nsetting out such facts as the provider considers relevant with\nrespect to acts or things done by the provider in order to comply\nwith the international production order.\n\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1) or (2):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "production orders by prescribed communications\nproviders\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is not an individual;\na manager of the provider may issue a written certificate signed by\nthe manager setting out such facts as the manager considers\nrelevant with respect to acts or things done by the provider in order\nto comply with the international production order.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is an individual;\nthe provider may issue a written certificate signed by the provider\nsetting out such facts as the provider considers relevant with\nrespect to acts or things done by the provider in order to comply\nwith the international production order.\n\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1) or (2):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-161-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-161-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-161-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b38f879ebd1b93869ea85dff3411a0d83b53161e494af7d8d867b96c4706b19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-161",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "161 Evidentiary certificates—compliance with international",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 282,
      "values:originalText": "production orders by prescribed communications\nproviders\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is not an individual;\na manager of the provider may issue a written certificate signed by\nthe manager setting out such facts as the manager considers\nrelevant with respect to acts or things done by the provider in order\nto comply with the international production order.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(b) the provider is an individual;\nthe provider may issue a written certificate signed by the provider\nsetting out such facts as the provider considers relevant with\nrespect to acts or things done by the provider in order to comply\nwith the international production order.\n\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1) or (2):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
