    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-163",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "163 Evidentiary certificates—interception",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-163"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.290",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of an interception agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 163\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the Organisation in accordance\nwith an international production order issued under\nclause 89; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 89.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certifying officer of an interception agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 163\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the Organisation in accordance\nwith an international production order issued under\nclause 89; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-163-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-163-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-163-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-163-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40cc877eff536edfbdc1ccbc23137f67226d2610f3d1f3b86a235d358700326e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-163",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "163 Evidentiary certificates—interception",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 290,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of an interception agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30; or\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 163\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 30.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 60.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of:\n\n(i) intercepted communications; or\n\n(ii) intercepted messages; or\n\n(iii) intercepted voice calls; or\n\n(iv) intercepted video calls;\n\nthat were made available to the Organisation in accordance\nwith an international production order issued under\nclause 89; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 89.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
