    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "164 Evidentiary certificates—stored communications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-164"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nissue a written certificate signed by the officer setting out such\nfacts as the officer considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of a copy of stored\ncommunications that were made available to the\nOrganisation in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 98; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 98.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nissue a written certificate signed by the officer setting out such\nfacts as the officer considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of a copy of stored\ncommunications that were made available to the\nOrganisation in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 98; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 98.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37e7a9141e709070b301b81f2724e6a7c36f641e2e03b1e2baa1f74c9e4bed9f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-164",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "164 Evidentiary certificates—stored communications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nissue a written certificate signed by the officer setting out such\nfacts as the officer considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 39.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the agency of a copy of stored communications\nthat were made available to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that\nwas disclosed to the agency in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 69.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to:\n\n(a) the receipt by the Organisation of a copy of stored\ncommunications that were made available to the\nOrganisation in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 98; or\n\n(b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data\nthat was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 98.\n\nInternational production orders  Schedule 1\nEvidentiary certificates  Part 12\n\nClause 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document."
    },
