    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-165",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165 Evidentiary certificates—telecommunications data",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-165"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.293",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of an enforcement agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 48.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 78.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications\ndata that was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 107.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certifying officer of an enforcement agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 48.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 78.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications\ndata that was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 107.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-165-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-165-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-165-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-165-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c3ad503c6f7a7dd1a8f5fa460d3a70b507275e1f8a5ddaa6ba3140bc36792844"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-165",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "165 Evidentiary certificates—telecommunications data",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 293,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying officer of an enforcement agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 48.\n\n(2) A certifying officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer\nconsiders relevant with respect to the receipt by the agency of\ntelecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in\naccordance with an international production order issued under\nclause 78.\n\n(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the\nperson setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with\nrespect to the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications\ndata that was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an\ninternational production order issued under clause 107.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2) or (3):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
