      "cml:integrityHash": "13e8eb5a4b6b6e9ef5db8601d31e6cc38830444a37c09ee8b880e6d59c47ea74",
      "skos:note": "Issue a written certificate with relevant facts to prescribed communications providers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-166-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166(1) Evidentiary certificates—Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 294,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may issue a written\ncertificate signed by the Australian Designated Authority setting\nout such facts as the Australian Designated Authority considers\nrelevant with respect to:\n\n(a) giving an international production order to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; or\n\n(b) giving an instrument of revocation of an international\nproduction order to a prescribed communications provider; or\n\n(c) giving an instrument of cancellation to a prescribed\ncommunications provider."
    },
    {
