    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166(4) Evidentiary certificates—Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-166-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.294",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If an international production order requires a prescribed\ncommunications provider to disclose telecommunications data to:\n\n(a) a relevant agency; or\n\n(b) the Organisation;\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the Australian\nDesignated Authority may issue a written certificate signed by the\nAustralian Designated Authority setting out such facts as the\nAustralian Designated Authority considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(c) the receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ntelecommunications data; or\n\n(d) anything done by the Australian Designated Authority for the\npurposes of ensuring that the telecommunications data was\npassed on to the agency or Organisation, as the case requires.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If an international production order requires a prescribed\ncommunications provider to disclose telecommunications data to:\n\n(a) a relevant agency; or\n\n(b) the Organisation;\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the Australian\nDesignated Authority may issue a written certificate signed by the\nAustralian Designated Authority setting out such facts as the\nAustralian Designated Authority considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(c) the receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ntelecommunications data; or\n\n(d) anything done by the Australian Designated Authority for the\npurposes of ensuring that the telecommunications data was\npassed on to the agency or Organisation, as the case requires.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9cf38f337b7125b567f9833ba91088a85bdeeb67fc382f5e0450f53a8f568661",
      "skos:note": "Issue written certificate with relevant facts about telecommunications data disclosure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-166-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166(4) Evidentiary certificates—Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 294,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If an international production order requires a prescribed\ncommunications provider to disclose telecommunications data to:\n\n(a) a relevant agency; or\n\n(b) the Organisation;\nindirectly via the Australian Designated Authority, the Australian\nDesignated Authority may issue a written certificate signed by the\nAustralian Designated Authority setting out such facts as the\nAustralian Designated Authority considers relevant with respect to:\n\n(c) the receipt by the Australian Designated Authority of the\ntelecommunications data; or\n\n(d) anything done by the Australian Designated Authority for the\npurposes of ensuring that the telecommunications data was\npassed on to the agency or Organisation, as the case requires."
    },
