    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166(5) Evidentiary certificates—Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-166-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.294",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2), (3) or (4):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2), (3) or (4):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cdb9a54e923c49a5a12b4e1beb78ab625789bd672ce45e704ed454add3e970ec",
      "skos:note": "A document purporting to be a certificate is prima facie evidence in a proceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-166-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166(5) Evidentiary certificates—Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 294,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubclause (1), (2), (3) or (4):\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-166-ss-5-norm",
