      "cml:conclusionText": "It is prima facie evidence in a proceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-167",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "167 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-167"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.296",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-167-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-167-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f8a22e784035842c80b8b287b8e1ce7d77b21f2564efea57736fa97b3eed061d",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from certain provisions for acts done in compliance with foreign country orders or requests under international agreements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-167",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "167 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 296,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-167-norm",
