    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "172(5) International production order issued in response to a telephone",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-172-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing\nperson under subclause (3):\n\n(a) the issuing person must:\n\n(i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled;\nand\n\n(b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant\nagency—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the\nOrganisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing\nperson under subclause (3):\n\n(a) the issuing person must:\n\n(i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled;\nand\n\n(b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant\nagency—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the\nOrganisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f05d7fb8f4ffd8bcaf8410e9acfbdce57ae9112b6bea9d5003405872986d7a2e",
      "skos:note": "Must inform relevant parties of cancellation",
      "dc:description": "instrument of cancellation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-172-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "172(5) International production order issued in response to a telephone",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing\nperson under subclause (3):\n\n(a) the issuing person must:\n\n(i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled;\nand\n\n(b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant\nagency—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the\nOrganisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority."
    },
    {
