    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "172(6) International production order issued in response to a telephone",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-172-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave the international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (3);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave the international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (3);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24d58345995e62d1b71d30a01e203c9cd9d76c9c5a3ee5413136e6e6d8ca5e22",
      "skos:note": "Duty to schedule international production order after cancellation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-172-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "172(6) International production order issued in response to a telephone",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) the Australian Designated Authority gave the international\nproduction order to the prescribed communications provider\nto whom the order is directed; and\n\n(b) the order was subsequently cancelled under subclause (3);\nthe Australian Designated Authority must:\n\nSchedule 1  International production orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-6"
