    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179 Delegation by the Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-179"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may, by writing, delegate any\nor all of the Australian Designated Authority’s functions or powers\nunder this Schedule to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nAttorney-General’s Department; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who holds, or is acting in, an Executive\nLevel 1 or 2 position in the Attorney-General’s Department.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee, acting SES employee and APS\nemployee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation\nunder subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions\nof the Australian Designated Authority.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may, by writing, delegate any\nor all of the Australian Designated Authority’s functions or powers\nunder this Schedule to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nAttorney-General’s Department; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who holds, or is acting in, an Executive\nLevel 1 or 2 position in the Attorney-General’s Department.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee, acting SES employee and APS\nemployee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation\nunder subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions\nof the Australian Designated Authority.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34ab8fc0be392aad41d1ae852b1e32edfb1eade1fea0caf749a2299585831e03"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-179",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179 Delegation by the Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may, by writing, delegate any\nor all of the Australian Designated Authority’s functions or powers\nunder this Schedule to:\n\n(a) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nAttorney-General’s Department; or\n\n(b) an APS employee who holds, or is acting in, an Executive\nLevel 1 or 2 position in the Attorney-General’s Department.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee, acting SES employee and APS\nemployee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation\nunder subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions\nof the Australian Designated Authority."
    },
