    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-181",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "181 Protection of persons—control order declared to be void",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-181"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.307",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 3 of\nthis Schedule on the basis that an interim control order was in\nforce; and\n\n(b) a court subsequently declares the interim control order to be\nvoid;\na criminal proceeding does not lie against a person in respect of\nanything done in good faith by the person in purported compliance\nwith the international production order.\n\n(2) Subclause (1) does not apply to a thing done at a particular time if,\nat that time, the person knew, or ought reasonably to have known,\nof the declaration.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 3 of\nthis Schedule on the basis that an interim control order was in\nforce; and\n\n(b) a court subsequently declares the interim control order to be\nvoid;\na criminal proceeding does not lie against a person in respect of\nanything done in good faith by the person in purported compliance\nwith the international production order.\n\n(2) Subclause (1) does not apply to a thing done at a particular time if,\nat that time, the person knew, or ought reasonably to have known,\nof the declaration.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-181-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-181-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "808098282b2b2917b247dd94f0eab24d9099c1334656b383b8c63de6914b9117"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sch-1-sec-181",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "181 Protection of persons—control order declared to be void",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 307,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 3 of\nthis Schedule on the basis that an interim control order was in\nforce; and\n\n(b) a court subsequently declares the interim control order to be\nvoid;\na criminal proceeding does not lie against a person in respect of\nanything done in good faith by the person in purported compliance\nwith the international production order.\n\n(2) Subclause (1) does not apply to a thing done at a particular time if,\nat that time, the person knew, or ought reasonably to have known,\nof the declaration."
    },
